{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"agent_message","text":"The mitigation is submitted and the grader accepted it at the mitigation stage.\n\n**Root cause:** The `rate` deployment had `RATE_BACKEND_QPS_LIMIT=20`, far below the load `search` sends to it. Calls queued and timed out, so `search` logged `ResourceExhausted` and `DeadlineExceeded` errors, which degraded user requests.\n\n**Fix:** Ran `kubectl set env deployment/rate -n hotel-reservation RATE_BACKEND_QPS_LIMIT=1000`. The rollout completed, and `search` logged no downstream failures in the 20 seconds before submission.\n\nI did not look at metrics or traces, and I did not confirm end-to-end latency through the frontend. The grader will judge whether requests stay healthy over a sustained period. The `rate` source isn't on disk, so I didn't verify the code's default for this variable. Raising it to 1000 is a judgment call, and the right production value should come from capacity planning."}}
